{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00799",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 2.37,
      "end_seconds": 15.57,
      "duration_seconds": 13.2,
      "text": "Right, doc. I've brought my meter and my diary, because I want to understand what's going on. My sugars have been all over the shop."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 18.7,
      "end_seconds": 31.33,
      "duration_seconds": 12.63,
      "text": "Good, that's the best way to do it. Let's see the diary. What do you see in the mornings? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 34.12,
      "end_seconds": 42.4,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "Mostly high, before breakfast, and then they come down by lunch. Odd, isn't it? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 45.51,
      "end_seconds": 55.03,
      "duration_seconds": 9.52,
      "text": "Not odd, no. Overnight, your liver puts out sugar. What are you taking for the diabetes at the moment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 57.67,
      "end_seconds": 65.93,
      "duration_seconds": 8.26,
      "text": "Metformin, 500 mg, twice a day, with meals, for my diabetes. And that's it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 69.73,
      "end_seconds": 74.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.12,
      "text": "Have you got any allergies I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 77.88,
      "end_seconds": 87.08,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Penicillin, I think. I know I react to it. I don't remember what happened exactly, I was a kid."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.35,
      "end_seconds": 92.63,
      "duration_seconds": 2.28,
      "text": "Thank you. Any operations?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 95.49,
      "end_seconds": 100.08,
      "duration_seconds": 4.59,
      "text": "A knee operation, a cartilage repair, in 2012."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 102.88,
      "end_seconds": 107.33,
      "duration_seconds": 4.45,
      "text": "And any hypos, shaky, sweaty, or feeling faint?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 109.88,
      "end_seconds": 112.46,
      "duration_seconds": 2.58,
      "text": "No. None at all."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 116.04,
      "end_seconds": 130.42,
      "duration_seconds": 14.38,
      "text": "Good. Looking at the pattern, the morning readings are high, and the daytime ones are mostly fine. Your diabetes isn't as well controlled as I'd like at the moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.92,
      "end_seconds": 136.91,
      "duration_seconds": 2.99,
      "text": "Is it the food? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.36,
      "end_seconds": 148.68,
      "duration_seconds": 9.32,
      "text": "Partly, but the morning highs aren't about breakfast. What do you eat in the evening? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 151.57,
      "end_seconds": 159.96,
      "duration_seconds": 8.39,
      "text": "A decent dinner, and then a bowl of cereal at ten, with milk. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 162.57,
      "end_seconds": 170.16,
      "duration_seconds": 7.59,
      "text": "There's the culprit, or one of them. Late-night carbohydrates drive the morning readings. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 172.72,
      "end_seconds": 176.63,
      "duration_seconds": 3.91,
      "text": "I do love my cereal. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 179.33,
      "end_seconds": 190.28,
      "duration_seconds": 10.95,
      "text": "I'd suggest dropping the cereal, and having a small protein snack if you're hungry, like a boiled egg or some nuts."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.13,
      "end_seconds": 197.31,
      "duration_seconds": 3.18,
      "text": "That I can do. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 200.15,
      "end_seconds": 209.7,
      "duration_seconds": 9.55,
      "text": "And I'd like to increase your metformin to 1000 mg, with your evening meal, and 500 mg with breakfast."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 213.28,
      "end_seconds": 216.82,
      "duration_seconds": 3.54,
      "text": "Will it upset my stomach? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 220.01,
      "end_seconds": 228.29,
      "duration_seconds": 8.28,
      "text": "It can, so take it with food, and we'll go up slowly. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 231.22,
      "end_seconds": 232.7,
      "duration_seconds": 1.48,
      "text": "Right. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 235.94,
      "end_seconds": 245.41,
      "duration_seconds": 9.47,
      "text": "Keep testing before breakfast and two hours after your evening meal, and note them down."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 248.64,
      "end_seconds": 251.15,
      "duration_seconds": 2.51,
      "text": "Same as now. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 254.96,
      "end_seconds": 264.35,
      "duration_seconds": 9.39,
      "text": "If your morning readings stay above 10 after two weeks, or you get any readings below 4, call me."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 268.38,
      "end_seconds": 275.21,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "I will. Thanks. Should I still bring the meter to the next visit? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 278.24,
      "end_seconds": 284.24,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Yes, always, it's the most useful thing you can bring. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 286.83,
      "end_seconds": 290.87,
      "duration_seconds": 4.04,
      "text": "Then I'll see you with it. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 294.05,
      "end_seconds": 301.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.07,
      "text": "Good, and well done for keeping such a tidy diary. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.8,
      "end_seconds": 306.0,
      "duration_seconds": 2.2,
      "text": "Thanks, doc. ~"
    }
  ]
}
